# The River Ivlis crossroads (data/locations/svalich_crossroads.json): the gallows and the signpost.
# The hanged man is Nicu, a young Vistana from the Tser Pool camp (stanimir.dialogue, luminita.dialogue). Cut him down
# and he stays dead; leave him, and after dark he and the old hanged dead in the field rise (crossroads_hanged_dead).

~ gallows
if flag.nicu_cut_down
Narrator: The gallows rope hangs empty, cut short above the knot. Beside the road, a mound of turned earth, marked with a board laid face down.
-> END
endif
if flag.crossroads_dead_cleared
-> remains
endif
if not flag.crossroads_gallows_seen
set crossroads_gallows_seen
quest the_hanged_vistana found
endif
cutscene crossroads_gallows
Narrator: A young man turns slowly on the rope, black hair across his face, a silver earring catching what light there is. A board hung round his neck says HORSE THIEF, in large and careful letters.
if night
Narrator: His fingers twitch. It could be the wind. There is no wind.
endif
if guest:ireena
Ireena: Father used to ride out and cut them down himself. He said a crossroads is no place to be left; the dead get confused about which road leads home.
endif
if guest:ismark
Ismark [weary]: Vistani, by the earring. Whoever did this was proud of their lettering.
endif
-> gallows_menu

~ gallows_menu
* Cut him down and bury him. -> cut_down
* [if not flag.nicu_body_examined] [Medicine DC 12] Look at the body. -> body_ok | body_fail
* [if not flag.nicu_token_taken] Take the earring, for his people. -> token
* Leave him. -> leave

~ body_ok
set nicu_body_examined
Narrator: Dead a day, two at most. Split knuckles: he fought them. The knot is a farmer's knot, tied fast and badly by somebody angry and in a hurry.
Narrator: And he is cold, colder than the dead should be, the way the ground is cold in the field behind the gallows. Something there is waiting for dark.
-> gallows_menu

~ body_fail
set nicu_body_examined
Narrator: A dead young man and a cheap rope. If there is more to read in him, the crows got to it first.
-> gallows_menu

~ token
set nicu_token_taken
Narrator: You work the earring free. It is a little silver horse's head, warm from nothing at all.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Not keeping it, before anyone asks. Old hands, new habits. It's going home.
approve wren_featherfoot +1 liriel_dawnsong +1: You took the hanged Vistana's earring home for his people
-> gallows_menu

~ leave
Narrator: You leave him turning. Behind you, the rope creaks once, as if he has shifted his weight.
approve liriel_dawnsong -1 godrick_pendlebrook -1: You left a hanged man turning on the gallows
-> END

~ cut_down
set nicu_cut_down
quest the_hanged_vistana buried
Narrator: The rope parts at the first cut. You lay him on the road, then dig beside it where the earth is soft, with blades and hands and whatever else will move dirt.
if not flag.nicu_token_taken
set nicu_token_taken
Narrator: Before the earth goes over him, someone thinks to take the silver earring. His people will want it.
endif
interject tag:veteran: Not my first roadside grave. Shallow is fine. Straight matters.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1 wren_featherfoot +1 kip_smudgewick +1: You cut down the hanged Vistana and gave him a grave
* [Cleric] Say the rites over him. -> rites
* [Religion DC 12] Say what words you can remember. -> rites | rites_fumbled
* Fill in the grave. -> buried

~ rites
set nicu_rites_said
Narrator: The words go down into the grave with him. Behind the gallows, one of the old mounds settles, like a sleeper turning over.
-> buried

~ rites_fumbled
Narrator: The words come out in the wrong order. You say them anyway. It is the meaning that counts, or so you have to hope.
-> buried

~ buried
Narrator: You mark the grave with the HORSE THIEF board, turned face down. It is the kindest thing anyone has done with it.
-> END

~ remains
Narrator: The rope hangs empty. What is left of the hanged man lies on the planks, where you put him down the second time.
* Bury what's left of him. -> bury_remains
* [if not flag.nicu_token_taken] Take the earring, for his people. -> remains_token
* Leave him. -> END

~ remains_token
set nicu_token_taken
Narrator: The silver earring is still there, a little horse's head. You work it free.
-> remains

~ bury_remains
set nicu_cut_down
Narrator: You bury him by the road. This time he stays where he is put.
if not flag.nicu_token_taken
set nicu_token_taken
Narrator: Someone keeps the silver earring back from the grave. His people will want it.
endif
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You buried the hanged Vistana by the road
-> END

~ signpost
Narrator: Four arms on a leaning post, the paint long gone and the names cut deep with a knife: BAROVIA east, VALLAKI and TSER POOL west, TSER FALLS north. The south arm has been sawn off, and someone has nailed a dead crow in its place.
if guest:ireena and not flag.ireena_crossroads
set ireena_crossroads
Ireena: Father said there was nothing past the crossroads but more Barovia. He was right. It's the same mud. I still want to see it.
if guest:ismark
Ismark: It's very good mud. Westward mud. I'm told the gentry prefer it.
endif
endif
interject class:rogue: The crow's fresh. Somebody keeps replacing it.
-> END
